# A circle drawn as 36 short sides. `sin` takes degrees, like `left` and `right`,
# so a side that fits a circle of this radius is 2 * radius * sin(half a turn
# over the number of sides). `//` divides whole numbers and `%` is what is left
# over, which is how every other side comes out red.
sides = 36
radius = 100
side = 2 * radius * sin(180 / sides)
turn = 360 // sides
for i from 1 to sides do
  color(if i % 2 == 0 then "red" else "blue" done);
  forward(side);
  right(turn)
done
